%S A398300 8,14,18,20,24,26,28,30,32,34,36,36,38,40,42,42,44,46,46,48,48,50,52,
%T A398300 52,54,54,56,56,58,58,60,60,62,62,64,64,64,66,66,68,68,70,70,70,72,72,
%U A398300 74,74,74,76,76,76,78,78,80,80,80,82,82,82,84,84,84,86,86,86,88,88,88
%N A398300 a(n) is the minimum possible sum of the numbers on all non-mine cells when n mines are placed on an infinite Minesweeper board (each non-mine cell's number is the count of mines among its up to 8 neighbors).
%C A398300 Equivalent to: place n mines (any distinct cells) on the infinite grid to minimize the total number of (mine, non-mine) adjacent pairs, where adjacency includes diagonals (king-move / Moore neighborhood).
%C A398300 This equals 8n - 2*M(n), where M(n) is the maximum number of edges in an induced subgraph of order n of the grid graph with diagonals added (vertex set Z^2, edges between points at Euclidean distance 1 or sqrt(2)). M(n) was conjectured by Taliceo and Fleron (2021) to equal 4n - ceil(sqrt(28n-12)), and this was proved by Vince (2024); see LINKS.
%C A398300 The optimal mine configurations are, loosely, almost-square blocks (approximately regular octagons in the limit).
%H A398300 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A398300/b398300.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A398300 Andrew Vince, <a href="https://doi.org/10.37236/12133">An Extremal Graph Problem on a Grid and an Isoperimetric Problem for Polyominoes</a>, Electronic Journal of Combinatorics, 31(2) (2024), #P2.5.
%F A398300 a(n) = 2*ceiling(sqrt(28*n - 12)).
%e A398300 a(4) = 20: placing 4 mines as a 2x2 block, every pair of the 4 mines is mutually king-adjacent (6 adjacent mine pairs), and each mine has 8 - 3 = 5 non-mine neighbors, giving 4*5 = 20 total (mine, non-mine) adjacent pairs, i.e. sum 20. No arrangement of 4 mines does better.
%t A398300 2*Ceiling[2*Sqrt[7*Range[100] - 3]] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Jul 31 2026 *)
%o A398300 (Python)
%o A398300 import math
%o A398300 def a(n): return 2*math.ceil(math.sqrt(28*n - 12))
%Y A398300 Cf. A027709 (analogous minimum-perimeter sequence for 4-neighbor adjacency, i.e. without diagonals).
%K A398300 nonn,easy,new
%O A398300 1,1
%A A398300 _Dimas Saputra_, Jul 25 2026
